  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #4.\n\nAdds Hermes as a first-class local usage source alongside OpenCode and Codex CLI.\n\n- reads Hermes session metrics from `~/.hermes/state.db`, table `sessions`\n- normalizes Hermes records into overview, models, daily chart, and usage history APIs\n- keeps total tokens as non-cache input + output while showing cache read/write separately\n- marks Hermes active only when the local state DB exists and documents the source contract\n- adds fixture-backed tests for missing-source behavior, aggregation, daily filtering, pricing normalization, and usage history\n\n## Validation\n\n- `uv run python -m unittest tests.test_app tests.test_readme -v`\n- `uv run python -m py_compile app.py scripts/snapshot_dashboard.py`\n- `scripts/review.sh`\n- `node --check /tmp/dashboard-inline.js`\n- Browser smoke at `http://127.0.0.1:8321/`: dashboard rendered with active OpenCode + Codex CLI + Hermes source cards, Hermes rows in model/history tables, and no browser console errors.\n",
